From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ios-blink-sideload <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:01:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iOS sideload: ad and content blocking with uBlock Origin's
 lists

Blocks ads, trackers and malware with Chromium's own subresource filter,
fed with filter lists compiled from uBlock Origin's default lists (uBlock
filters, EasyList, EasyPrivacy, Peter Lowe's list, Online Malicious URL
Blocklist) by compile_filters.py at build time.

- ios/web/content/adblock/adblock_ruleset: on first launch, parses the
  bundled adblock_filters.txt with Chromium's EasyList parser
  (components/subresource_filter/tools/rule_parser) and indexes it with
  subresource_filter::RulesetIndexer. The index is cached in
  Library/Caches/SideloadAdblock and verified on later launches; it is
  rebuilt when the list or the Chromium version changes.
- AdblockRenderFrameObserver: installs a WebDocumentSubresourceFilterImpl
  on every web document (and worker), so Blink blocks matching subresource
  loads; Chrome normally only does this on sites Safe Browsing flags.
  Element hiding: inserts a user-origin stylesheet with the site-specific
  `##` rules for the document's site (from the index), plus the generic
  ones (compiled stylesheet) in main frames.
- AdblockNavigationThrottle: blocks and collapses matching iframes.
- $document, $genericblock, $elemhide and $generichide allowlist rules are
  honoured and inherited by child frames.
- chrome://flags: "Ad and content blocking" and "Ad blocking: hide ad
  placeholders", both on by default.
- GN arg ios_sideload_adblock_lists_dir: directory with the compiled
  lists, bundled into the app. Unset means no lists and no blocking.

Not supported (dropped at compile time, never broadened): scriptlets
(##+js), HTML filtering (##^), procedural cosmetic filters, $redirect,
$removeparam, $csp, $denyallow, regex filters, entity domains, strict
blocking of top-level pages.

Status: written against Chromium 3313f827 + patches 0001-0038 and applies
cleanly on top of them; NOT yet compiled or run (needs a Mac).
